{"seq":2,"slug":"government-revenue","title":"第二章 政府收入与税收","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/economics/public-finance/government-revenue","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"taxation-principles","title":"大学财政学 — 税收原则与税制设计","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/economics/public-finance/government-revenue/taxation-principles","wordCount":1760,"readingTime":8},{"seq":2,"slug":"tax-incidence","title":"大学财政学 — 税收归宿","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/economics/public-finance/government-revenue/tax-incidence","wordCount":1632,"readingTime":7},{"seq":3,"slug":"major-tax-types","title":"大学财政学 — 主要税种解析","url":"/l-doc-books/education/university/economics/public-finance/government-revenue/major-tax-types","wordCount":1710,"readingTime":7}],"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"第二章-政府收入与税收\">第二章 政府收入与税收</h1><p>税收是现代政府最主要的收入来源，也是财政学技术含量最高的部分。本章讨论一套好税制应当遵循的原则（效率与公平），分析&quot;税收归宿&quot;这一最反直觉也最重要的概念——名义上谁交税，和实际上谁承担税负，往往是两回事。</p>\n<p>我们还会逐一拆解个人所得税、增值税、企业所得税等主要税种的设计逻辑，让你能读懂税率表、理解累进税与比例税的区别，并学会用经济学工具评判一项税收政策的得失。</p>\n"}